{"step_index":6327,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-24T01:18:30Z","thinking":"The code uses `res.latency`, but the Python function returns `\"latency_ms\"`. Updating to `res.latency_ms` is essential for correct latency display. Also, a stopped server necessitates a warning message: \"⚠️ Server '${serverKey}' is stopped. Please click 'Start Server' (تشغيل السيرفر) first.\", accompanied by a toast notification.\n\n\nThe CSS defines the application layout, establishing the body, main layout container, and sidebar with their respective styling properties.  The sidebar's properties include width constraints, background, border, flexbox layout, and overflow handling. The brand section within the sidebar is styled with padding, flexbox, alignment, border, color, and drop-shadow effects.\n\n\nThis section defines the visual styling of the navigation menu, individual navigation items, and the sidebar footer, using flexbox for layout and transitions for hover effects. The `.text-danger` class indicates a styling for error messages, likely including a hover effect, while the `.server-status-card` class defines styling for server status display.\n\n\nThe provided CSS dictates the visual presentation of server status cards within a grid layout, defining hover effects and status indicators.  A running server is visually distinguished by a green indicator with a glow, while a stopped server uses a red indicator. The main content area utilizes flexbox to manage layout and overflow behaviors.  The screen section within the main content is hidden initially, with slide-in animation, styling, and overflow handling.\n\n\nThe code defines the layout for the AI servers management screen using a grid, ensuring responsiveness across different screen sizes with a flexible column count. Server cards are styled with borders, shadows, and hover effects, visually distinguishing active providers with a primary-colored border and enhanced shadow.\n\n